# t15-pdf: what the lead applies for nr-office-pdf-ocr, nr-office-pdf-preview and nr-office-pdf-writer (hot files)

The in-crate parts (module lines, mixdog-office-pdf Cargo.toml edges, the worker's registration and its Cargo.toml) are applied and
committed on branch t-t15-pdf. The three original fragments are deleted.

## native/core/Cargo.lock (regenerate with `cargo update --workspace --offline`; no new package)

mixdog-office-pdf: add dependencies flate2, mixdog-office-com, mixdog-office-crypto, reqwest, sha2, zip (dev: flate2, sha2, zip).
mixdog-exthost-worker: add dependencies mixdog-fonts, mixdog-office-com, mixdog-office-pdf, mixdog-ooxml (mixdog-rt was already one; its
dev-dependency `test-support` is now also reached through the worker's own `test-support` feature).
No cycle: none of the four depends on mixdog-exthost-worker.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml

Run the repository's hakari check after the lock; take its output (tokio features `sync`/`macros`/`rt-multi-thread` on mixdog-office-pdf,
flate2/reqwest/zip features).

