## native/core/crates/mixdog-app-server-daemon/src/compose.rs, fn native_ext_methods

The worker now registers the office PDF backend (the worker's `OfficeEngine` (methods/document_engine.rs)) for document.preview and
document.previewPages, and `document.libreOfficeStatus` is answered as before. One thing is not in the worker: the Noto font provisioner
(`prepare_fonts` after `document.installLibreOffice`) lives in the daemon's domain_seams/office_fonts.rs, which a worker cannot depend on;
the worker's `prepare_fonts` is empty and says so. Therefore the route change that loses nothing keeps ONLY the install with the script
worker until the provisioner is moved into a crate the worker links (then drop that term too):

    /// The methods the Rust worker answers. The image methods stay with the script worker until the image corpus passes whole, and
    /// `document.installLibreOffice` until the font provisioner it runs after an install is reachable from the worker.
    pub fn native_ext_methods() -> Vec<&'static str> {
        mixdog_exthost_worker::native_methods()
            .into_iter()
            .filter(|method| !method.starts_with("image.") && *method != "document.installLibreOffice")
            .collect()
    }

(If the lead prefers the one-line change of the review note, drop `&& !method.starts_with("document.")` only; the install then runs in
the worker without the font provisioning that Node's did after it.)

## Process exit

The worker registers `Registry::on_exit` (scratch removal of every preview and `Soffice::process().shutdown`). Registry has one exit hook
slot: another task that sets one (office sessions) must call both.

## Test commands that prove the worker answers the document methods as the Node worker did

From native/core, with CARGO_TARGET_DIR and CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true set:

    pwsh -NoLogo -NoProfile -File D:\mixdog-build\tools\cargo-gate.ps1 nextest run -p mixdog-exthost-worker --features mixdog-exthost-worker/test-support
    pwsh -NoLogo -NoProfile -File D:\mixdog-build\tools\cargo-gate.ps1 nextest run -p mixdog-office-pdf
    pwsh -NoLogo -NoProfile -File D:\mixdog-build\tools\cargo-gate.ps1 nextest run -p mixdog-app-server-daemon

The first runs, through the pool over `ext_worker_dev` (which registers the real engine), tests/document_twin.rs (the four methods are
served; a PDF previews in place; the root, type, page, width and password guards; a PDF page is rasterised by the registered engine and
answered as Node's previewPages: 401 x 567 PNG at maxWidth 400), the handler-layer tests of src/methods/document.rs (scripted engine:
rasterised pages, the pin of an unlocked document) and src/methods/soffice.rs (status probe and install). The second is the engine itself
against the recordings (twin_preview, preview_render, preview_password). A LibreOffice or Microsoft Office conversion of a real document
needs the application and is not run by any test.
